Yes. In `packages/core/EventManager.ts` the diff changes `destinationCalendar` to an array and adds:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  ...
}
```

When `evt.destinationCalendar` is `undefined`, `null`, or an empty array, `mainHostDestinationCalendar` will be `undefined`, and `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will throw at runtime. This is a concrete correctness bug introduced by the change to array semantics. The other new uses in the diff generally keep `?.` when dereferencing (`mainHostDestinationCalendar?.externalId`, etc.), so this instance has indeed lost the safety guard.
